# Project Context — Support Ticket Management System

## What This Project Is

Full-stack internal ticket management app built as a JS AI Capability Exercise.
Three-tier monorepo: `client/` (React + Vite + TS) + `server/` (Express + TS) + PostgreSQL (Prisma).

## Approved Tech Stack (do not change)

| Layer | Technology |
| ----- | ---------- |
| Frontend | React, Vite, TypeScript, React Router, Tailwind CSS |
| Backend | Node.js, Express, TypeScript, Zod |
| Database | PostgreSQL, Prisma ORM |
| Testing | Vitest, Supertest |

## Document Authority (resolve conflicts in this order)

1. `docs/requirement-analysis.md` — FR/BR/AC business authority
2. `tool-specific/cursor-workflow/spec.md` — technical blueprint
3. `tool-specific/cursor-workflow/acceptance-criteria.md` — verification checklist
4. `tool-specific/cursor-workflow/tasks.md` — sprint execution order
5. `tool-specific/cursor-workflow/cursor-rules-or-instructions.md` — engineering rules

## Non-Negotiables

| Topic | Rule |
| ----- | ---- |
| Status changes | `PATCH /api/tickets/:id/status` only — general PATCH rejects `status` → 400 |
| State machine | `server/src/services/statusTransition.ts` — 5 valid transitions, backend-enforced |
| Search | Title + description, case-insensitive partial (`ILIKE`) |
| Auth | None in v1 — document as known limitation |
| Delete | No ticket delete in v1 |
| Secrets | Never in Git — `.env` gitignored; only `.env.example` committed |
| Stretch | No stretch features until AC-01–AC-18 all pass |
